.TH "GLESHA" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glesha \- encrypted archives and cloud backups
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glesha [global options] COMMAND [arguments] [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create encrypted archives, keep snapshot histories in cloud buckets, and restore files without overwriting existing files.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Back up and recover
.TP
.B create SET PATH...
Register sources and a backup destination
.TP
.B run SET
Create and upload a backup
.TP
.B restore SET \-\-into DIR
Restore files without overwriting existing files
.TP
.B import SET
Register an existing archive
.SS Inspect
.TP
.B list
List locally known sets and IDs
.TP
.B status [SET]
Show backup state, sizes, and estimated cost
.TP
.B history SET
List snapshots
.TP
.B browse SET
List files in a snapshot
.TP
.B catalog sync [SET]
Discover sets or synchronize one catalog
.TP
.B catalog unlock SET
Open a downloaded encrypted catalog locally
.SS Manage
.TP
.B configure SET
Change saved settings or bind local sources
.TP
.B retry SET
Resume pending work
.TP
.B cleanup SET|\-\-all
Remove eligible local archive copies
.TP
.B move SET \-\-from A \-\-to B
Copy history and switch destinations
.TP
.B storage\-class SET
Change an AWS archive's storage class
.TP
.B check \-\-to REMOTE...
Test bucket access
.TP
.B state migrate
Move legacy local state to the current location
.SS Standalone files
.TP
.B archive PATH...
Create an encrypted archive
.TP
.B decrypt FILE
Decrypt to compressed tar
.TP
.B extract FILE \-\-into DIR
Extract into a new directory
.TP
.B upload FILE \-\-to REMOTE...
Upload a file
.TP
.B download KEY \-\-from REMOTE
Download a file
.SS Help and version
.TP
.B help [COMMAND [ACTION]]
Show options and examples
.TP
.B version
Show version and build revision
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-format FORMAT
Result format: plain or json; status also supports table and csv (default: plain).
.TP
.B \-\-progress MODE
Progress on stderr: auto, plain, or off (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-\-config FILE
TOML settings file.
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir DIR
Local state directory; overrides catalog.directory.
.TP
.B \-\-env FILE
Load credentials; existing process variables take priority.
.TP
.B \-\-color MODE
Color mode: auto, yes, or no (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-L, \-\-log\-level LEVEL
Diagnostic verbosity: debug, info, warn, error, or silent (default: info).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show this command's help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version and build revision.
.SH OUTPUT
Results and tables go to stdout. Activity, prompts, warnings, and errors go to stderr.
Use \-\-format=json for result records, one per line.
Catalog sync records use output version 3; other results retain version 2.
JSON diagnostics and progress use separate version 1 records on stderr; neither stream contains ANSI controls.
Use \-\-progress=off to disable progress. In plain output, redirected stderr or TERM=dumb uses step lines.
Informational text is plain. Errors are red, warnings yellow, and ready states green when color is enabled.
Color defaults to terminal detection. Human formatting may change independently of JSON records.
.SH BUCKET ACCESS
Without \-\-from or \-\-to, configured and saved provider choices apply. An explicit selection limits all bucket access to their union, including catalogs and registry copies.
Include every required bucket explicitly. Selecting buckets does not make an operation read-only.
.SH LOCAL STATE
Use \-\-state\-dir DIR to override catalog.directory for one invocation. This selects local state, not cloud buckets.
Empty legacy registries do not block existing default state. Nonempty locations are never merged automatically; use state migrate or choose a location explicitly.
.SH PASSPHRASES
Catalog and archive passphrases are separate. catalog sync downloads encrypted metadata; catalog unlock SET reads a cached catalog locally.
Restore requires the archive passphrase as well. File flags can supply passphrases; a dash reads stdin. Hidden prompts support Ctrl+C.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An operation or configuration failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command usage or an unknown set.
.TP
.B 3
Pending work must be finished first.
.TP
.B 4
Catalog histories conflict.
.TP
.B 130
Operation cancelled.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha create docs ~/Documents \-\-to b2
glesha run docs
glesha catalog sync \-\-from b2
glesha catalog unlock SET
glesha help restore
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha-catalog (1),
.BR glesha-status (1),
.BR glesha-restore (1)
